{
  "title": "Prader-Willi Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4105/prader-willi-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 16 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Prader-Willi Syndrome is a congenital condition caused by a partial chromosome 15 deletion that presents with obesity, failure to thrive, mental retardation, hip dysplasia, and scoliosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with physical examination at birth and genetic testing to identify a missing portion of chromosome 15.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach to address orthopedic manifestations, cognitive abnormalities, and metabolic abnormalities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1 in 25,000 births",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
